<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-TNT announces board changes.</title>
<headline>RTRS-TNT announces board changes.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>TNT Ltd said on Thursday it had appointed Ad Scheepbouwer as chairman of the transport group following the resignation of Fred Millar.</p>
<p>TNT also said managing director David Mortimer had resigned from his position but remained a director of the company. He will be replaced by Andre Cohen and John Yates, who will be joint managing directors of the Australian transport group.</p>
<p>The board changes follow the takeover of TNT by Koninklijke PTT Nederland NV (KPN). KPN said on Wednesday it had 96.3 percent of TNT. Scheepbouwer is an executive of KPN.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
